    ],
    "justification": "The reduction checks inside the maintained \\(T\\ge3\\) model that the cycle correction vanishes and that cohort-mean PPML becomes an explicit multi-post multiplicative ratio.",
    "gap": "Ciani and Fisher (2019) establish the canonical two-period multiplicative DiD ratio; this proposition gives the admissible fixed-\\(T\\), \\(T\\ge3\\), acyclic analogue that pools all post-adoption cells.",
    "consumer": "Users with one treated cohort and a never-treated cohort can compute the multi-post proportional effect directly and omit covariance-cycle estimation.",
    "proof_tex": "When \\(q=0\\), \\(R\\) has no columns. The variance projection therefore gives \\(h_{\\mathrm{CM}}=h^{\\star}\\), the estimator definition makes no correction, and the empty quadratic form gives \\(\\Gamma=0\\).\n\nLet \\(C=\\{2,\\infty\\}\\). There are \\(1+T\\) untreated edges, so\n\\[\nq=(T+1)-2-T+1=0.                                       \\tag{1}\n\\]\nThe untreated graph is the canonical tree. On \\(\\mathcal E_N\\), \\(X\\) is square and nonsingular and \\(\\widehat P_U\\) is diagonal positive. Hence the PPML score implies\n\\[\n\\overline Y_U=\\exp(X\\widehat\\beta).                     \\tag{2}\n\\]\nUnder \\(\\widehat b_1=1\\), equation (2) gives\n\\[\n\\widehat a_2=\\overline Y_{21},\\qquad\n\\widehat a_\\infty=\\overline Y_{\\infty1},\\qquad\n\\widehat b_t=\n\\frac{\\overline Y_{\\infty t}}{\\overline Y_{\\infty1}}\n\\quad(2\\le t\\le T).                                     \\tag{3}\n\\]\nOnly cohort \\(2\\) is treated, at periods \\(2,\\ldots,T\\). Thus\n\\[\n\\widehat A=p_2\\sum_{t=2}^T\\overline Y_{2t},\n\\qquad\n\\widehat B\n=p_2\\overline Y_{21}\n\\sum_{t=2}^T\n\\frac{\\overline Y_{\\infty t}}{\\overline Y_{\\infty1}}.  \\tag{4}\n\\]\nThe denominator is positive on \\(\\mathcal E_N\\). Cancelling \\(p_2>0\\) in (4) gives the claimed explicit ratio, and the empty correction gives \\(\\widehat\\theta_{\\mathrm{eff}}=\\widehat\\theta_{\\mathrm{CM}}\\).",
